  "readmeFile": "README.NuGet.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v0.8.0: new commands devop-dk customer count, product count, and purchase vendor count print the number of matching records (or {\"count\": n} with --json), for example to show import progress; they take the list command's filters plus --modified-since/-m, where an ISO date such as 2025-01-01 is midnight UTC (a date-time needs Z or an offset). A filter the DK Plus count cannot apply (customer --name and --email; product --item-code, --alias-item-code and --deleted; vendor --postal-code, --group and --modified-before) fails with exit code 2 naming the option, and nothing is sent. The vendor count is the row count of the dkERP vendor table APVEND, which includes rows without a vendor number that the vendor list skips, so it is an upper bound (verified live on 2026-10-27: 384 counted, 383 listed plus 1 skipped). New: purchase vendor group list and count read the dkERP table APGROUPS, and customer group count and product group count count ARGROUPS and INGROUPS (-m sends the table's modified time). New top-level devop-dk vendor runs every purchase vendor command (devop-dk vendor group count -m 2026-02-01); the purchase vendor path keeps working. purchase vendor list now also takes -m for --modified-after.",
